id: 1692
event: message.updated
data: {"type": "message.updated", "sequence": 1692, "run_id": "run_39688b3495bc4b32", "data": {"id": "e39de21a-2ff9-4cbe-8c79-9338047fe685", "run_id": "run_39688b3495bc4b32", "kind": "tool", "position": 1688, "revision": 1692, "parent_tool_use_id": null, "agent_call_id": null, "data": {"name": "Read", "input": "{\"file_path\": \"[workspace]\", \"limit\": 25, \"offset\": 155}", "output": "155\t\n156\t## Reproducibility\n157\t\n158\tAll analysis was performed using Python 3.11 with pandas, numpy, and scipy. The complete analysis pipeline consists of scripts in `output/`:\n159\t\n160\t1. `output/analysis_01_explore_data.py` — Data loading and structural exploration\n161\t2. `output/analysis_02_core_findings.py` — Core statistical tests (linear regression, sign-change detection, DME trends)\n162\t3. `output/analysis_03_figures.py` — Figure CSV generation and cross-comparisons\n163\t4. `output/analysis_04_deep.py` — Angle-resolved analysis, polynomial fitting, leave-one-out robustness\n164\t5. `output/analysis_fix_energy_alignment.py` — **Corrected** energy-grid alignment with cubic spline interpolation and perturbation analysis\n165\t6. `working/analysis_round3_angle_resolved.py` — Round 3 corrected angle-resolved analysis on spline-aligned grids\n166\t\n167\tIndependent replication was performed by a general-purpose sub-agent that wrote its own analysis scripts from scratch. The sub-agent code was deleted after execution (per leaf-agent constraint), but all results are preserved in `output/independent_dme_results.json`, `output/independent_angular_coeff_results.json`, and `output/independent_wigner_results.json`.\n168\t\n169\tTo reproduce: run each script in sequence from the project root directory:\n170\t```bash\n171\tcd [workspace]\n172\tpython3 output/analysis_01_explore_data.py\n173\tpython3 output/analysis_02_core_findings.py\n174\tpython3 output/analysis_03_figures.py\n175\tpython3 output/analysis_04_deep.py\n176\tpython3 output/analysis_fix_energy_alignment.py\n177\t```\n178\t\n179\tAll output artifacts are in `output/`. The input data in `data/` must remain unchanged.", "status": "completed", "is_async": false, "tool_use_id": "call_9b2f9038ae714fc19995c386"}, "created_at": "2026-10-16T09:52:34.194071+00:00", "updated_at": "2026-10-16T09:52:34.868195+00:00"}}

